---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import { projectsData } from '../../data/projects';

const project = projectsData.find(p => p.id === 1)!;
---
<Layout
  title={project.metaTitle}
  description={project.metaDescription}
  currentPage="project-detail"
>
  <!-- Hero -->
  <section class="pt-20 pb-20 text-center px-6 hero-section">
    <h1 class="text-3xl md:text-4xl lg:text-5xl font-serif font-bold mb-4 hero-title">CoffeeNanny Lviv</h1>
    <p class="text-lg text-gray-600 max-w-xl mx-auto hero-subtitle">UX/UI Design &middot; Client Research &middot; Rapid MVP &middot; Wix</p>
  </section>

  <!-- Project Detail -->
  <section class="section py-20 px-6">
    <div class="container mx-auto max-w-3xl">
      <div class="mb-8">
        <a href="/projects.html" class="text-sm font-medium text-link link-arrow-back">Back to All Projects</a>
      </div>

      <p class="text-gray-500 uppercase tracking-wide text-sm font-medium mb-2">Complete Project</p>
      <h2 class="text-3xl md:text-4xl font-serif font-bold mb-8">CoffeeNanny Lviv Franchise Website</h2>

      <div class="grid md:grid-cols-2 gap-10 items-start mb-16">
        <div>
          <img src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1600880292203-757bb62b4baf?crop=entropy&cs=tinysrgb&fit=max&fm=jpg&q=80&w=800" alt="CoffeeNanny Lviv Franchise Website" class="rounded-lg shadow-lg w-full h-auto object-cover" loading="lazy">
        </div>
        <div class="space-y-6">
          <p class="text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">
            CoffeeNanny is a service that helps families find trusted nannies for their children &mdash; by the hour or for longer periods, both in-home and onsite. When I came on board through a local Lviv agency, the franchise had a critical trust problem: without a proper website, serious clients had no way to verify the service or feel confident entrusting their children to a new provider.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-600 font-medium">
            Social media worked for discovery, but families needed transparency, clear pricing, and a professional channel to make an informed decision. I led the entire digital rebuild &mdash; from UX audit and client interviews to Figma design and a rapid Wix MVP.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Context -->
      <div class="mb-12">
        <h2 class="text-xl font-serif font-bold mb-4 section-title-mb-6">Context</h2>
        <p class="text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-4">
          The original franchise site &mdash; built for the Kyiv office &mdash; went down during the full-scale invasion. The Lviv franchise needed a new digital presence urgently, but more importantly, they needed one that actually worked for their local market. Research revealed the core issue wasn't just missing functionality &mdash; it was <strong>trust</strong>.
        </p>
        <p class="text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-4">
          Most local leads came through Instagram, but Instagram alone couldn't close serious clients. There was also a new audience: many displaced families who had fled to Lviv from other regions were searching for nannies directly on <strong>Google</strong> &mdash; they had no local Instagram network to discover CoffeeNanny through. Without a website, this entire segment was completely unreachable.
        </p>
        <p class="text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">
          Families needed to see pricing, understand how the service worked, and feel confident before trusting someone with their child. A proper website wasn't just nice to have &mdash; it was the only channel that could serve both local and displaced families effectively.
        </p>
      </div>

      <!-- Approach -->
      <div class="mb-12">
        <h2 class="text-xl font-serif font-bold mb-4 section-title-mb-6">Approach</h2>
        <div class="space-y-6">
          <div>
            <h3 class="text-base font-semibold mb-2">1. UX Audit &amp; Competitive Research</h3>
            <p class="text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">
              I started with a UX audit of the previous franchise-wide site. Key finding: it felt generic &mdash; no local presence, no Lviv-specific content, no clear trust signals for a childcare service. I also researched direct and indirect competitors to identify what they did well and where CoffeeNanny could differentiate. This analysis shaped our positioning and content strategy from day one.
            </p>
          </div>
          <div>
            <h3 class="text-base font-semibold mb-2">2. Client &amp; Stakeholder Interviews</h3>
            <p class="text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">
              I interviewed existing clients to understand what drove their trust, how they discovered the service, and what nearly stopped them from booking. Conversations with the franchise owner clarified business priorities and the roadmap.
            </p>
          </div>
          <div>
            <h3 class="text-base font-semibold mb-2">3. Design in Figma + AI-Assisted Style Exploration</h3>
            <p class="text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">
              Based on research insights, I designed the full site in Figma &mdash; information architecture, wireframes, and high-fidelity UI. To speed things up, I used one of the first AI design tools available in 2022 to generate style variants and explore different visual directions rapidly. This let us converge on the right look much faster than iterating manually.
            </p>
          </div>
          <div>
            <h3 class="text-base font-semibold mb-2">4. MVP on Wix</h3>
            <p class="text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">
              To ship fast, I built the MVP directly on Wix &mdash; leveraging its CMS, SEO tools, and hosting to get the site live in days rather than weeks. This allowed the franchise to immediately start generating inquiries.
            </p>
          </div>
          <div>
            <h3 class="text-base font-semibold mb-2">5. Data-Informed Iteration</h3>
            <p class="text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">
              After launch, I analysed user behaviour and conversion data to refine the experience &mdash; A/B testing messaging, adjusting the booking flow, and improving content based on what actually drove inquiries.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Result -->
      <div class="mb-12">
        <h2 class="text-xl font-serif font-bold mb-4 section-title-mb-6">Result</h2>

        <p class="text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-4">
          The business went from near-collapse to stable growth. The new site launched in days and became a working client-generation engine. Four years later, the site is still live and the franchise has expanded to <strong>9 cities</strong> across Ukraine.
        </p>

        <h3 class="text-base font-semibold mb-2">Traffic Growth (May 2022 &rarr; 2026)</h3>
        <p class="text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-4">
          The site launched with almost no traffic and a <strong>90% bounce rate</strong>. Within months it was attracting thousands of visitors per month &mdash; a <strong>20&times; increase</strong> in traffic driven entirely by organic search and social media, with no paid advertising.
        </p>

        <h3 class="text-base font-semibold mb-2">Engagement Quality</h3>
        <p class="text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-4">
          The bounce rate dropped from <strong>90% at launch to ~55%</strong> &mdash; a clear signal that the UX and content structure worked: visitors were finding what they needed instead of leaving immediately. Average session duration grew to <strong>2&ndash;4 minutes</strong>, indicating serious engagement from potential clients.
        </p>

        <h3 class="text-base font-semibold mb-2">Traffic Sources (Lifetime)</h3>
        <div class="overflow-x-auto mb-4">
          <table class="min-w-full text-sm text-gray-700 border-collapse">
            <thead>
              <tr class="border-b border-gray-200">
                <th class="text-left py-2 pr-4 font-semibold">Source</th>
                <th class="text-right py-2 pl-4 font-semibold">Share</th>
              </tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody>
              <tr class="border-b border-gray-100"><td class="py-2 pr-4">Instagram (organic social)</td><td class="text-right py-2 pl-4">37%</td></tr>
              <tr class="border-b border-gray-100"><td class="py-2 pr-4">Google (organic search)</td><td class="text-right py-2 pl-4">36%</td></tr>
              <tr class="border-b border-gray-100"><td class="py-2 pr-4">Direct (bookmarks / typed URL)</td><td class="text-right py-2 pl-4">19%</td></tr>
              <tr class="border-b border-gray-100"><td class="py-2 pr-4">Facebook</td><td class="text-right py-2 pl-4">6%</td></tr>
              <tr class="border-b border-gray-200"><td class="py-2 pr-4">Other (Bing, DuckDuckGo, ChatGPT, etc.)</td><td class="text-right py-2 pl-4">2%</td></tr>
            </tbody>
          </table>
        </div>

        <p class="text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-4">
          Instagram was the top acquisition channel (37%), but <strong>Google organic search was nearly tied at 36%</strong> &mdash; proving the site's SEO and information architecture effectively captured search demand from families looking for nannies. Direct traffic at 19% demonstrated growing brand recognition: people remembered the URL and came back.
        </p>

        <p class="text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">
          The project proved that a lean, research-informed approach can keep a business alive under extraordinary pressure &mdash; and that a well-designed MVP can become a permanent, revenue-generating asset.
        </p>
      </div>

      <!-- Role -->
      <hr class="divider mb-8">
      <div>
        <h2 class="text-base font-serif font-bold mb-2">My Role</h2>
        <p class="text-gray-600 leading-relaxed">
          UX/UI Designer &amp; Product Designer &mdash; competitive research, client &amp; stakeholder interviews, information architecture, Figma design with AI-assisted style exploration, Wix MVP development, analytics review and iteration.
        </p>
      </div>

      <!-- Live Site -->
      <div class="mt-8">
        <h2 class="text-base font-serif font-bold mb-2">Live Site</h2>
        <p class="text-gray-600 leading-relaxed">
          <a href="https://www.coffeenanny.lviv.ua/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-link link-external">https://www.coffeenanny.lviv.ua/</a>
        </p>
      </div>

    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>
